# Normalize every text file to LF in the repository, whatever the contributor's
# platform or core.autocrlf setting. The build inputs and the shell scripts are
# line-ending sensitive: a CRLF tests/integration.sh fails on Linux and macOS
# with "bad interpreter: No such file or directory", and a CRLF Makefile breaks
# every recipe. Normalizing on commit is cheaper than debugging that later.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF so they work when checked out on Windows.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary fixtures and artifacts must never be normalized.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.o binary
*.a binary
